      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It's October 31. I want to schedule an event for October 31. You'd think it's easy, right? Wrong.\n\nThe event form defaults to November 1, written in the american format because screw my locale.\n\nI try to change the month first. It is reverted, because October 1 is in the past.\n\nOk, let's try to change the day. Reverted, because November doesn't have 31 days.\n\nFuck, well, let's use the little dropdown popup. October 31 is greyed out, and doesn't work when I click on it. Oh, right, the time the page loaded in October 31 has already passed. Let's click to set the time of the event first.\n\n...October 31 is still greyed out? Except, now it works when I click it. 🤷‍♂️ \n\nNow let's set the ending time for the event. The event form defaults to November 1... 😫",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
